{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they shall make Me a sanctuary, etc.</b> One must know why He called it <b>mikdash</b>, and immediately retracted and called it mishkan, as it is written <b>the pattern of the mishkan</b>." "It appears that His saying <b>and they shall make Me a sanctuary</b> is an inclusive positive commandment for all times, whether in the wilderness or upon their entry into the land, throughout all generations that Israel would be there. And Israel were obligated to do so even in the exiles, except that we find that HaShem forbade all places from the time the Temple was built, as He said (Deuteronomy 12:9) ״כִּי לֹא בָאתֶם עַד עָתָּה אֶל הַמְּנוּחָה וְאֶל הַנַּחֲלָה״. Therefore He did not say ״and they shall make a mishkan,״ which would have been understood to mean that this commandment was said only for that time alone. And after He commanded in general terms, He specified what was to be made in the wilderness, which is not a place for building with stone — that they should make a mishkan in the arrangement described. And you will find that the Rambam wrote in chapter 1 of Hilkhot Beit HaBechirah: It is a positive commandment to make a house for HaShem, as it is written ״וְעָשׂוּ לִי מִקְדָּשׁ״ — end quote, and his reasoning is the change of language, as we have written. Further, His saying <b>and they shall make Me a sanctuary</b> intends that from the time they make it for His name, blessed be He, as He said ״for Me,״ even though the Shekhinah has not yet dwelt in it, it is nevertheless a mikdash and the legal status of holiness applies to it." "<b>And I shall dwell among them.</b> And He did not say ״within it,״ to say that the place which they consecrate for His dwelling shall be in the midst of the children of Israel, so that they would surround the mishkan with the four banners. Or perhaps these words are a response to what Israel yearned for (Numbers Rabbah 2:5) when they saw at Mount Sinai that the Holy One, blessed be He, was surrounded by banners of angels and He was a sign among them, and they yearned and desired to have it so among them as well; therefore the response came from the Examiner of hearts, and He said <b>and they shall make Me a sanctuary and I shall dwell</b> likewise <b>among them</b>."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:33:18.977888648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}